                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "My game time with Thief series is more than 100 hours for thief 1,  2 and 3, and i think this review is a a bit too late :) . For what its worth, you did a great job Looking Glass studios and all the dev's who worked on this game, shame after this game decision to change the game engine and the story overhaul plummeted my interest in this genre, if you could just stick with the horror/thriller and the same atmosphere of the first game it would be a legend like Witcher today. This second installment of thief series is setting a less darker world and this is where we see Garett mingling in politics in his own way, however from gameplay perspective it adds a few extra elements to the gameplay mechanics which makes it slightly more fun. It is certainly not a let down, and story is - maybe not as interesting as the first one, still thriling in its own way. The overhauled engine and slightly better graphics also is fun compared to thief 1, i have to admit I grew up with this game, I found every crevice every hole every secret this game thows in as a challenge. If they think about doing a total ReMake of Thief games, they should and I stress this out so badly - just do it on Thief 1 and no more. Thief 2 is the game of missed opportunities and bad choices, but that doesnt make it not fun, I just feel it could be a legend but it lost that chance. thats all i have to say.",
